{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --stat; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '90,365p'; rg -n 'bounded|read-file|utf|regular' src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc; sed -n '55,80p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; rg -n 'parse-int|--port' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\"","aggregated_output":" docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md |   4 +-\n src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc                |  46 +-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc            | 859 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc           |  40 +-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc           | 181 +++++--\n src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc          |  74 ++-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc          |   7 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md      | 105 ++++-\n test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj    | 206 +++++++-\n test/yin/repl/main_test.cljc          | 135 +++++-\n test/yin/repl/state_test.cljc         |  28 ++\n 11 files changed, 1505 insertions(+), 180 deletions(-)\n    90\t  \"Why a reader cannot hydrate `manifest` into a directory whose own HEAD\n    91\t   already names `recovered`, or nil.  Hydration never replaces an index\n    92\t   the directory holds.\"\n    93\t  [dir manifest recovered]\n    94\t  (when (and manifest recovered (not= manifest recovered))\n    95\t    (str dir \" already holds an index (HEAD names \" recovered \"); hydrate \"\n    96\t         manifest \" into an empty directory\")))\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t;; heads.edn (5.7)\n   101\t;; =============================================================================\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn- read-edn\n   104\t  [text]\n   105\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string text)\n   106\t     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n   107\t     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- read-one\n   111\t  \"The one EDN form `text` holds, or ::unreadable: a trailing form, a\n   112\t   truncated suffix and an empty text are refused, as on every host's\n   113\t   `read-string` alone they are not.  The text is read inside a vector\n   114\t   closed by a sentinel no file can predict, so the first form that\n   115\t   reads is the whole vector only when the text is exactly one complete\n   116\t   form (whitespace and comments around it allowed).\"\n   117\t  [text]\n   118\t  (let [end (keyword \"yin.repl.dht\" (str \"end-\" (random-uuid)))\n   119\t        ;; a newline ends a trailing comment; no whitespace precedes the\n   120\t        ;; closer (ClojureDart's reader refuses one)\n   121\t        forms (read-edn (str \"[\" text \"\\n\" end \"]\"))]\n   122\t    (if (and (vector? forms) (= 2 (count forms)) (= end (second forms)))\n   123\t      (first forms)\n   124\t      ::unreadable)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn parse-heads\n   128\t  \"The records `text`, a `heads.edn` read from `path`, holds:\n   129\t   `{:records {:version 1 :heads {principal trace}}}`, or `{:refusal\n   130\t   text}` when it is not exactly one readable EDN form or not a version-1\n   131\t   heads file.\n   132\t   Never throws.  The records themselves are verified by\n   133\t   `yin.vm.linker.head/follow`.\"\n   134\t  [path text]\n   135\t  (let [data (try (read-one text)\n   136\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   137\t                    ::unreadable))]\n   138\t    (cond\n   139\t      (= ::unreadable data)\n   140\t      {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it is not readable EDN\")}\n   141\t\n   142\t      (not (and (map? data) (= 1 (:version data)) (map? (:heads data))\n   143\t                (= #{:version :heads} (set (keys data)))))\n   144\t      {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it is not a version-1 heads file\")}\n   145\t\n   146\t      :else {:records data})))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn render-heads\n   150\t  \"The text of `records`: one EDN map, with no whitespace before a\n   151\t   closing bracket (ClojureDart's reader refuses one).\"\n   152\t  [records]\n   153\t  (str (pr-str records) \"\\n\"))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn- read-bounded\n   157\t  \"At most `limit` bytes of the file at `path`, one more when it holds\n   158\t   more, or nil when no entry exists there.  Never reads the whole of a\n   159\t   larger file into memory.\"\n   160\t  [path limit]\n   161\t  #?(:cljd (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n   162\t             (if (.existsSync f)\n   163\t               (let [raf (.openSync f)]\n   164\t                 (try (.readSync raf (inc limit))\n   165\t                      (finally (.closeSync raf))))\n   166\t               ;; a directory or a dangling link is an entry, not absence\n   167\t               (when (or (.existsSync (dart-io/Directory. path))\n   168\t                         (.existsSync (dart-io/Link. path)))\n   169\t                 (throw (ex-info \"it is not a readable file\" {})))))\n   170\t     :clj (let [p (java.nio.file.Paths/get path (make-array String 0))]\n   171\t            (when-not (java.nio.file.Files/notExists\n   172\t                        p (into-array java.nio.file.LinkOption\n   173\t                                      [java.nio.file.LinkOption/NOFOLLOW_LINKS]))\n   174\t              (with-open [in (java.nio.file.Files/newInputStream\n   175\t                               p (make-array java.nio.file.OpenOption 0))]\n   176\t                (.readNBytes in (int (inc limit))))))\n   177\t     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")]\n   178\t             (when (or (.existsSync fs path)\n   179\t                       (try (.lstatSync fs path) true\n   180\t                            (catch :default _ false)))\n   181\t               (let [fd (.openSync fs path \"r\")\n   182\t                     buf (js/Buffer.alloc (inc limit))]\n   183\t                 (try\n   184\t                   (loop [off 0]\n   185\t                     (let [n (.readSync fs fd buf off (- (inc limit) off) nil)\n   186\t                           off' (+ off n)]\n   187\t                       (if (and (pos? n) (< off' (inc limit)))\n   188\t                         (recur off')\n   189\t                         (.subarray buf 0 off'))))\n   190\t                   (finally (.closeSync fs fd))))))))\n   191\t\n   192\t\n   193\t(defn- byte-length\n   194\t  [bs]\n   195\t  #?(:cljd (.-length bs)\n   196\t     :clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n   197\t     :cljs (.-length bs)))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn- decode-utf8\n   201\t  \"`bs` as text, strictly: invalid UTF-8 throws, never decodes to a\n   202\t   replacement character.\"\n   203\t  [bs]\n   204\t  #?(:cljd (.convert (convert/Utf8Decoder. .allowMalformed false) bs)\n   205\t     :clj (str (.decode (doto (.newDecoder java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets/UTF_8)\n   206\t                          (.onMalformedInput\n   207\t                            java.nio.charset.CodingErrorAction/REPORT)\n   208\t                          (.onUnmappableCharacter\n   209\t                            java.nio.charset.CodingErrorAction/REPORT))\n   210\t                        (java.nio.ByteBuffer/wrap ^bytes bs)))\n   211\t     :cljs (.decode (js/TextDecoder. \"utf-8\" #js {:fatal true}) bs)))\n   212\t\n   213\t\n   214\t(defn read-heads\n   215\t  \"The persisted head records of the store directory `dir`: `{:records\n   216\t   r}`, an empty version-1 record when no `heads.edn` exists, or\n   217\t   `{:refusal text}`: a file that cannot be read, holds more than\n   218\t   `heads-max-bytes`, is not valid UTF-8, or is not exactly one\n   219\t   version-1 record.  Never throws.\"\n   220\t  [dir]\n   221\t  (let [path (str dir \"/\" heads-file)\n   222\t        bs (try (read-bounded path heads-max-bytes)\n   223\t                (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   224\t                  {::failed (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))\n   225\t        text (when (and (some? bs) (not (map? bs))\n   226\t                        (<= (byte-length bs) heads-max-bytes))\n   227\t               (try (decode-utf8 bs)\n   228\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   229\t                      ::invalid)))]\n   230\t    (cond\n   231\t      (nil? bs) {:records {:version 1 :heads {}}}\n   232\t      (map? bs) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it cannot be read (\"\n   233\t                               (::failed bs) \")\")}\n   234\t      (nil? text) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it holds more than \"\n   235\t                                 heads-max-bytes \" bytes\")}\n   236\t      (= ::invalid text) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path\n   237\t                                        \": it is not valid UTF-8\")}\n   238\t      :else (parse-heads path text))))\n   239\t\n   240\t\n   241\t;; =============================================================================\n   242\t;; The board and the deposit (5.4)\n   243\t;; =============================================================================\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn- ring\n   246\t  [n]\n   247\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   248\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n   249\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key n})))\n   250\t\n   251\t\n   252\t(defn- deposit-head!\n   253\t  \"Deposit the trace of `manifest`, read from `store`, on `board`; a\n   254\t   refusal is appended to `notes` for the step to print.\"\n   255\t  [{:keys [board key store notes]} manifest]\n   256\t  (let [r (try (head/deposit! board key manifest\n   257\t                              (space.index/read-datoms store manifest))\n   258\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   259\t                 {:status :refused :reason :yin.head/unreadable\n   260\t                  :manifest manifest :detail (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))]\n   261\t    (when (= :refused (:status r))\n   262\t      (stream/append! notes r))\n   263\t    r))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn- publisher\n   267\t  \"The board composition of a publishing node: a key, a socket (peers)\n   268\t   and `:publish?` (5.4), or nil.\"\n   269\t  [{:keys [peers publish?]} key base]\n   270\t  (when (and (map? key) (:seed key) (:public key) publish? (seq peers))\n   271\t    (let [notes (ring 64)]\n   272\t      {:board (head/board)\n   273\t       :key key\n   274\t       :principal (sign/principal (:public key))\n   275\t       :store base\n   276\t       :notes notes\n   277\t       :notes-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   278\t                       (stream/cursor notes stream/anchor-newest))})))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t;; =============================================================================\n   282\t;; Opening the store\n   283\t;; =============================================================================\n   284\t\n   285\t(defn followed-principals\n   286\t  \"The principal ids, `ed25519:<hex>`, a DHT store spec follows.\"\n   287\t  [spec]\n   288\t  (mapv #(sign/principal (:principal %)) (:follow spec)))\n   289\t\n   290\t\n   291\t(defn- checked-follow\n   292\t  \"The `:follow` entries of `spec`, each `{:principal hex :host h :port\n   293\t   p}` with a loopback literal host, one per principal; throws a refusal\n   294\t   otherwise.\"\n   295\t  [{:keys [follow peers]}]\n   296\t  (let [refuse #(throw (ex-info % {:follow follow}))]\n   297\t    (when-not (or (nil? follow) (vector? follow))\n   298\t      (refuse \"the followed principals must be a vector\"))\n   299\t    (doseq [{:keys [principal host port] :as f} follow]\n   300\t      (when-not (and (map? f) (string? principal)\n   301\t                     (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]{64}\" principal))\n   302\t        (refuse (str \"--dht-follow names a principal by 64 lowercase \"\n   303\t                     \"hexadecimal characters, not \" (pr-str principal))))\n   304\t      (when-not (head.ws/loopback? host)\n   305\t        (refuse (str \"--dht-follow \" principal \"@\" host \":\" port\n   306\t                     \": the head board is followed on loopback only\")))\n   307\t      (when-not (and (integer? port) (<= 1 port 65535))\n   308\t        (refuse (str \"--dht-follow \" principal \": the port must be 1 to \"\n   309\t                     \"65535, not \" (pr-str port)))))\n   310\t    (when (and (seq follow) (empty? peers))\n   311\t      (refuse (str \"--dht-follow needs a --dht-peer: a followed head's \"\n   312\t                   \"index is fetched over the DHT\")))\n   313\t    (when-not (= (count follow) (count (distinct (map :principal follow))))\n   314\t      (refuse \"--dht-follow names each principal once: one source each\"))\n   315\t    (vec follow)))\n   316\t\n   317\t\n   318\t(defn- heads-records\n   319\t  \"The records of `<dir>/heads.edn` when `follow` is not empty, read\n   320\t   before the node binds anything; a file that cannot be read as one\n   321\t   version-1 record refuses startup naming it.\"\n   322\t  [dir follow]\n   323\t  (when (seq follow)\n   324\t    (let [{:keys [records refusal]} (read-heads dir)]\n   325\t      (when refusal\n   326\t        (throw (ex-info (str refusal \"; move it aside to follow from no head\")\n   327\t                        {:dir dir})))\n   328\t      records)))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t(defn- follower-of\n   332\t  \"The follower of `follow` on `node`, restored from the persisted\n   333\t   `records` before any connection: `[follower node]`, or `[nil node]`\n   334\t   when nothing is followed.  A record that fails refuses startup naming\n   335\t   it.\"\n   336\t  [node dir follow records]\n   337\t  (if (empty? follow)\n   338\t    [nil node]\n   339\t    (let [path (str dir \"/\" heads-file)]\n   340\t      (try\n   341\t        (head/follow node {:follow (mapv #(sign/principal (:principal %))\n   342\t                                         follow)\n   343\t                           :heads records})\n   344\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   345\t          (if-some [reason (:yin.head/refused (ex-data e))]\n   346\t            (throw (ex-info (str \"heads file \" path \": \" (ex-message e)\n   347\t                                 \" (\" reason \"); remove that record to \"\n   348\t                                 \"follow it from no head, dropping its \"\n   349\t                                 \"rollback floor\")\n   350\t                            {:dir dir :reason reason}))\n   351\t            (throw e)))))))\n   352\t\n   353\t\n   354\t(defn- compose\n   355\t  \"The store handle of `open`, over the joined `node`: the publisher's\n   356\t   board, the follower restored from `records`, a pinned hydration, and\n   357\t   the HEAD write that announces and deposits.\"\n   358\t  [node base {:keys [dir manifest] :as checked} follow records\n   359\t   {:keys [key ws write-heads!]}]\n   360\t  (let [pub (publisher checked key base)\n   361\t        [follower node] (follower-of node dir follow records)\n   362\t        node (cond-> (assoc node ::dir dir ::ws ws)\n   363\t               pub (assoc ::publisher pub)\n   364\t               follower (assoc ::follower follower\n   365\t                               ::follow\n82:               (str/trim (.readFileSync ^js fs path \"utf8\"))))))\n375:                       (try (write-fully! fs fd (js/Buffer.from text \"utf8\"))\n388:(defn read-file-text\n       \"yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md), but composing a sink into \"\n       \"this shell is not, so the flags are rejected rather than ignored\"))\n\n\n(defn- parse-int\n  \"The decimal integer `text` names, or nil: total on every host.  At\n   most 15 digits, so the value is exact on every host (below 2^53) and\n   no host parser can overflow; a longer number is nil, which each flag\n   refuses as data.\"\n  [text]\n  (when (and (string? text) (re-matches #\"-?\\d{1,15}\" text))\n    #?(:cljd (int/parse text)\n       :cljs (js/parseInt text 10)\n       :clj (Long/parseLong text))))\n\n\n(defn parse-peer\n  \"A `--dht-peer` value, `host:port` or `[v6-host]:port`, as the DHT's\n   bootstrap contact `{:host h :port p}`.  The host must be an IP\n   literal: the DHT resolves no names.\"\n  [text]\n  (let [[_ v6 v4 port] (re-matches #\"(?:\\[([^\\]]+)\\]|([^:\\[\\]]+)):(\\d+)\"\n                                   (str text))\n        host (or v6 v4)\n        port (parse-int port)]\n    (cond\n59:(defn- parse-int\n79:        port (parse-int port)]\n124:        port (parse-int port)]\n326:  (or (parse-int text)\n527:          \"--port\" (recur (nnext args)\n529:                                              (let [n (parse-int p)]\n533:                                                           (str \"--port takes a \"\n539:          \"--host\" (throw (ex-info (str \"--host is gone: --port serves on all \"\n611:  \"`--port` listens on every interface: loopback and the machine's own IP.\"\n629:  \"This machine's address for `--port`'s banner and advertised host.\n657:  \"Compose the served endpoint for `--port`, or nil when no port was asked for.\n693:   \"  --port n          serve this shell to other shells over WebSockets, on\"\n695:   \"  --headless        no prompt, endpoint only; needs --port\"\n918:   input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  A `--port` process\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '400,455p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '620,870p'; rg -n 'simulated|before-rename|bounded|utf|trailing|gap' test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc; sed -n '1080,1225p' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj; cat collab/1791273851396-repl-engineer-head-h3-r2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log | tail -75\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '400,455p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '620,870p'; rg -n 'simulated|before-rename|bounded|utf|trailing|gap' test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc; sed -n '1080,1225p' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj; cat collab/1791273851396-repl-engineer-head-h3-r2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log | tail -75\"","aggregated_output":"   400\t\n   401\t   `opts`: `:key`, the publisher key `{:seed :public}`, which makes a\n   402\t   publishing node deposit its head; `:ws`, the host WebSocket seam\n   403\t   `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (yin.repl.host) the board is served and\n   404\t   dialed over; `:write-heads!`, `(fn [dir name text])`, the atomic file\n   405\t   replace `heads.edn` is written with (`dao.space.store.fs` by\n   406\t   default).\"\n   407\t  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n   408\t  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads!]}]\n   409\t   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n   410\t                 manifest bind!]\n   411\t          :as checked} (store/checked-spec spec)\n   412\t         follow (checked-follow checked)\n   413\t         base (durable/open dir)]\n   414\t     (try\n   415\t       (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n   416\t                                     (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n   417\t         (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n   418\t       (let [records (heads-records dir follow)\n   419\t             node (dht/join {:local base\n   420\t                             :peers peers\n   421\t                             :publish? publish?\n   422\t                             :bind-host bind-host\n   423\t                             :bind-port bind-port\n   424\t                             :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n   425\t                             :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})]\n   426\t         ;; from here the node holds a socket: every refusal closes it\n   427\t         (try\n   428\t           (compose node base checked follow records\n   429\t                    {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})\n   430\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   431\t             (dht/close! node)\n   432\t             (throw e))))\n   433\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   434\t         (store/close! base)\n   435\t         (throw e))))))\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\t(defn without-runner\n   439\t  \"The store handle the shell keeps: `open`'s answer without the node,\n   440\t   which the shell carries as its own `:dht`.  Any other handle is\n   441\t   answered as it is.\"\n   442\t  [handle]\n   443\t  (dissoc handle :dht))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(defn follower\n   447\t  \"The head follower the shell's DHT `node` carries, or nil when it\n   448\t   follows nothing.\"\n   449\t  [node]\n   450\t  (get node ::follower))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t(defn close!\n   454\t  \"Release what the head composition holds on the shell's node: the\n   455\t   board's listener and every dial.  Idempotent enough for an exit: a\n   620\t          \"dht: this host has no WebSocket listener: no head board, no token\"\n   621\t          (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n   622\t               (address-text host port) \": no board, no join token; \"\n   623\t               \"choose another --dht-port\"))])]))\n   624\t\n   625\t\n   626\t(defn- step-board\n   627\t  \"Advance the board's endpoint, print the token once when it is bound,\n   628\t   and print each deposit refusal: `[pub lines]`.\"\n   629\t  [pub node events now]\n   630\t  (let [bound (some #(when (= :bound (::dht/event %)) %) events)\n   631\t        [pub lines] (if (and bound (nil? (:server pub)))\n   632\t                      (serve-board pub (::ws node) (:host bound) (:port bound))\n   633\t                      [pub nil])\n   634\t        before (get-in pub [:server :status])\n   635\t        server (when (:server pub) (head.ws/serve-step (:server pub) now))\n   636\t        pub (cond-> pub server (assoc :server server))\n   637\t        [host port] (:listen pub)\n   638\t        lines (cond-> (vec lines)\n   639\t                (and (= :serving (:status server)) (not (:token? pub)))\n   640\t                (conj (str \"dht: join token: \"\n   641\t                           (join-token host port (:public (:key pub)))))\n   642\t\n   643\t                (and (= :refused (:status server)) (not= :refused before))\n   644\t                (conj (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n   645\t                           (address-text host port) \": no board, no join \"\n   646\t                           \"token; choose another --dht-port\")))\n   647\t        pub (cond-> pub (= :serving (:status server)) (assoc :token? true))\n   648\t        ;; a gap means refusals were evicted unread: adopt its recovery\n   649\t        ;; cursor, say so, and drain what the ring still holds\n   650\t        [notes lost? cursor] (loop [notes [] lost? false\n   651\t                                    cursor (:notes-cursor pub)]\n   652\t                               (let [r (stream/next (:notes pub) cursor)]\n   653\t                                 (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   654\t                                   :dao.stream/ok (recur (conj notes\n   655\t                                                               (:dao.stream/value r))\n   656\t                                                         lost?\n   657\t                                                         (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   658\t                                   :dao.stream/gap (recur notes true\n   659\t                                                          (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   660\t                                   [notes lost? cursor])))]\n   661\t    [(assoc pub :notes-cursor cursor)\n   662\t     (-> lines\n   663\t         (cond-> lost? (conj (str \"dht: more head trace refusals arrived \"\n   664\t                                  \"than could be kept; the oldest were not \"\n   665\t                                  \"reported\")))\n   666\t         (into (map (fn [{:keys [reason manifest]}]\n   667\t                      (str \"dht: the head trace of \" manifest \" was not \"\n   668\t                           \"deposited: \" reason)))\n   669\t               notes))]))\n   670\t\n   671\t\n   672\t(defn- hydrated\n   673\t  \"Install the loaded remote index as this directory's: HEAD first, then\n   674\t   the indexer, exactly as a restart's recovery is installed.  A\n   675\t   publisher deposits the hydrated HEAD's trace once (5.4).\"\n   676\t  [shell node]\n   677\t  (let [manifest (::hydrating node)\n   678\t        recovery {:manifest manifest :datoms (dht/loaded-datoms node manifest)}]\n   679\t    ((:head-fn (dht/local node)) manifest)\n   680\t    (when-some [pub (::publisher node)]\n   681\t      (deposit-head! pub manifest))\n   682\t    (-> shell\n   683\t        (update :indexer index/rehydrate recovery)\n   684\t        (assoc :index-recovery recovery\n   685\t               :dht (dissoc node ::hydrating)))))\n   686\t\n   687\t\n   688\t;; =============================================================================\n   689\t;; Following (5.3, 5.5, 5.7)\n   690\t;; =============================================================================\n   691\t\n   692\t(defn- next-delay\n   693\t  [follower delay]\n   694\t  (if delay\n   695\t    (min (* 2 delay) (:repair-max-ticks follower))\n   696\t    (:repair-ticks follower)))\n   697\t\n   698\t\n   699\t(defn- drop-dial\n   700\t  \"Close the dial of a link and schedule the next one after its delay;\n   701\t   the last failure reported is kept.\"\n   702\t  [follower link now]\n   703\t  (when-some [d (:dial link)] (head.ws/close! d))\n   704\t  (let [delay (next-delay follower (:delay link))]\n   705\t    {:due (+ now delay) :delay delay :failed (:failed link)}))\n   706\t\n   707\t\n   708\t(defn- lost-reason\n   709\t  \"What ended a lost dial, as one keyword: the remote's reason, or the\n   710\t   outcome.\"\n   711\t  [d]\n   712\t  (let [o (:outcome d)]\n   713\t    (or (:dao.stream.remote/reason o) (:dao.stream/outcome o) :lost)))\n   714\t\n   715\t\n   716\t(defn- dial-line\n   717\t  \"The line a dial failure prints when it differs from the last one.\"\n   718\t  [principal {:keys [host port]} failure]\n   719\t  (str \"dht: cannot follow \" principal \" at \" (address-text host port) \": \"\n   720\t       (case failure\n   721\t         :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   722\t         \"that endpoint serves no head board for this principal\"\n   723\t         :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone \"the connection was refused or closed\"\n   724\t         :yin.head/no-answer \"the board did not answer\"\n   725\t         :yin.head.ws/no-connector \"this host has no WebSocket dialer\"\n   726\t         (str failure))\n   727\t       \"; dialing it again\"))\n   728\t\n   729\t\n   730\t(defn- step-link\n   731\t  \"Advance the dial of `principal`'s board: compose one when due, step\n   732\t   it, hand a fresh reflection to the follower, and redial a dial that\n   733\t   is lost or still resolving after its delay (the host owns its\n   734\t   liveness: `yin.vm.linker.head.ws/dial` composes no resend).  Only\n   735\t   the address the principal was given is dialed.  Answers `[follower\n   736\t   link failure]`, `failure` the keyword that ended a dial this step,\n   737\t   or nil.\"\n   738\t  [follower ws source link now]\n   739\t  (cond\n   740\t    (and (nil? (:dial link)) (some? (:due link)) (< now (:due link)))\n   741\t    [follower link nil]\n   742\t\n   743\t    (nil? (:dial link))\n   744\t    (let [d (if-some [connect! (:connect! ws)]\n   745\t              (head.ws/dial {:principal (sign/principal (:principal source))\n   746\t                             :host (:host source)\n   747\t                             :port (:port source)\n   748\t                             :connect! connect!})\n   749\t              {:status :refused :reason :yin.head.ws/no-connector})]\n   750\t      (if (= :refused (:status d))\n   751\t        [follower (drop-dial follower link now) (:reason d)]\n   752\t        [follower (assoc link :dial d :since now :handle nil) nil]))\n   753\t\n   754\t    :else\n   755\t    (let [d (head.ws/dial-step (:dial link))\n   756\t          link (assoc link :dial d)\n   757\t          h (head.ws/handle d)]\n   758\t      (cond\n   759\t        (and h (not (identical? h (:handle link))))\n   760\t        [(head/attach follower (sign/principal (:principal source)) h)\n   761\t         (assoc link :handle h :delay nil :failed nil)\n   762\t         nil]\n   763\t\n   764\t        (= :lost (:status d))\n   765\t        [follower (drop-dial follower link now) (lost-reason d)]\n   766\t\n   767\t        (and (= :resolving (:status d))\n   768\t             (< (+ (:since link) (next-delay follower (:delay link))) now))\n   769\t        [follower (drop-dial follower link now) :yin.head/no-answer]\n   770\t\n   771\t        :else [follower link nil]))))\n   772\t\n   773\t\n   774\t(defn- step-links\n   775\t  \"Step every principal's dial: `[follower links lines]`, one line per\n   776\t   change of a dial's failure, never one per attempt.\"\n   777\t  [follower node now]\n   778\t  (let [{:keys [sources links]} (::follow node)]\n   779\t    (reduce (fn [[follower links lines] [p source]]\n   780\t              (let [[follower link failure] (step-link follower (::ws node)\n   781\t                                                       source (get links p)\n   782\t                                                       now)\n   783\t                    fresh? (and failure (not= failure (:failed link)))]\n   784\t                [follower\n   785\t                 (assoc links p (cond-> link failure (assoc :failed failure)))\n   786\t                 (cond-> lines fresh? (conj (dial-line p source failure)))]))\n   787\t            [follower links []]\n   788\t            sources)))\n   789\t\n   790\t\n   791\t(defn- persist\n   792\t  \"5.7 steps 2 and 3 for `principal`'s confirmed `trace`: replace\n   793\t   `heads.edn` with it in its place, and only when that returned,\n   794\t   install it.  A write that fails installs nothing and waits for the\n   795\t   repair delay.  Answers `[follower node waiting events]`.\"\n   796\t  [follower node waiting principal trace now]\n   797\t  (let [{:keys [write!]} (::follow node)\n   798\t        dir (::dir node)\n   799\t        failed (try (write! dir heads-file\n   800\t                            (render-heads (head/records follower principal\n   801\t                                                        trace)))\n   802\t                    nil\n   803\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   804\t                      (or (ex-message e) (str e))))]\n   805\t    (if failed\n   806\t      (let [delay (next-delay follower (get-in waiting [principal :delay]))]\n   807\t        [follower node\n   808\t         (assoc waiting principal {:trace trace :due (+ now delay)\n   809\t                                   :delay delay})\n   810\t         [{:yin.head/event :unpersisted :principal principal :trace trace\n   811\t           :detail failed :delay delay}]])\n   812\t      (let [[follower node events] (head/install follower node principal\n   813\t                                                 trace)]\n   814\t        [follower node (dissoc waiting principal) events]))))\n   815\t\n   816\t\n   817\t(defn- retry-waiting\n   818\t  \"Write again each confirmed head whose write failed, once its delay\n   819\t   has passed and while it is still the principal's confirmed candidate.\"\n   820\t  [follower node waiting now]\n   821\t  (reduce (fn [[follower node waiting events] [p {:keys [trace due]}]]\n   822\t            (let [cand (get-in (head/heads follower) [p :candidate])]\n   823\t              (cond\n   824\t                (not (and (= :confirmed (:state cand)) (= trace (:trace cand))))\n   825\t                [follower node (dissoc waiting p) events]\n   826\t\n   827\t                (< now due) [follower node waiting events]\n   828\t\n   829\t                :else\n   830\t                (let [[follower node waiting more]\n   831\t                      (persist follower node waiting p trace now)]\n   832\t                  [follower node waiting (into events more)]))))\n   833\t          [follower node waiting []]\n   834\t          waiting))\n   835\t\n   836\t\n   837\t(defn- linked-registry\n   838\t  \"`{name manifest-address}` of the modules the shell's VM linked.\"\n   839\t  [shell]\n   840\t  (into {}\n   841\t        (keep (fn [[n e]] (when (some? (:address e)) [n (:address e)])))\n   842\t        (some-> (get-in shell [:vm :modules]) module/module-entries)))\n   843\t\n   844\t\n   845\t(defn moved\n   846\t  \"The linked names of the shell's session whose resolved address\n   847\t   differs now (`yin.vm.linker.head/moved`): derived, stored nowhere.\"\n   848\t  [shell node]\n   849\t  (head/moved (ld/names node (link/authority (:link-source shell)))\n   850\t              (linked-registry shell)))\n   851\t\n   852\t\n   853\t(defn- moved-lines\n   854\t  \"The line of 5.7 for each linked name an installed head moved: only\n   855\t   moves that were not already standing before this step's installs\n   856\t   (`before`, the node then), so a name is reported once per new\n   857\t   address, and nothing is stored.\"\n   858\t  [shell before node installed]\n   859\t  (when (seq installed)\n   860\t    (let [heads (str/join \", \"\n   861\t                          (map (fn [{:keys [principal trace]}]\n   862\t                                 (str principal \" seq \"\n   863\t                                      (get-in trace [:yin.head/envelope\n   864\t                                                     :yin.head/seq])))\n   865\t                               installed))\n   866\t          standing (set (map (juxt :name :resolved) (moved shell before)))]\n   867\t      (into []\n   868\t            (comp (remove #(contains? standing [(:name %) (:resolved %)]))\n   869\t                  (map (fn [{n :name :keys [linked resolved]}]\n   870\t                         (str \"dht: \" n \" moved: linked \" linked\n486:(defn- crash-before-rename\n492:                      {:before-rename (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"crashed before the rename\" {})))}))\n504:(deftest a-simulated-crash-restarts-at-the-head-heads-edn-holds\n525:    (testing \"simulated crash before the write: the restart is at the old\n543:                     :b (reader w key dir-b {:write! crash-before-rename}))\n564:    (testing \"simulated crash between the write and the install: the restart\n638:             [\"a trailing form\" \"{:version 1 :heads {}} garbage\"\n661:                              \"a trailing form\" \"a truncated second form\"\n751:;; heads.edn is read bounded and strictly UTF-8\n772:(deftest heads-edn-is-bounded-and-strict-utf-8\n799:        (write-heads! dir (str \"; the heads\\n\" empty-text \"  ; trailing\\n\\n\"))\n    (is (await-next p \"(reset)\" #\"reset$\") (transcript p))\n    (is (await-next p \"(require (quote my.lib))\" #\"^(yin> )*'my\\.lib$\")\n        (transcript p))\n    (is (await-next p \"(my.lib/f 1)\" #\"^(yin> )*4301$\")\n        (str \"(reset) then require links the new module\\n\" (transcript p)))))\n\n\n(deftest\n  ^:slow a-reader-follows-the-publisher-s-head-across-processes\n  (let\n    [storing {::jing.dht/publish? true\n              ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes (* 64 1024 1024)}\n     anchor (start-anchor! storing)\n     dirs (vec (repeatedly 3 temp-dir))\n     key-file (str (temp-dir) \".key\")\n     peer #(str \"127.0.0.1:\" %)\n     procs (atom [])]\n    (is (nil? (:failure anchor)) (:failure anchor))\n    (when-not\n      (:failure anchor)\n      (try\n        (main/keygen! key-file)\n        (let\n          [x (:port anchor)\n           a-args [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (dirs 0)) \"--dht-peer\" (peer x)\n                   \"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-key\" key-file]\n           a1 (spawn! \"publisher-a\" a-args)\n           _ (swap! procs conj a1)\n           pa (bound-port a1)\n           token (some->> (await-line a1 token-line startup-ms)\n                          (re-find token-line)\n                          second)\n           public (second (re-find #\"/([0-9a-f]{64})$\" (str token)))\n           principal (str \"ed25519:\" public)]\n          (testing \"A prints the join token once its board is bound\"\n            (is (some? pa) (transcript a1))\n            (is (= (str \"yin:127.0.0.1:\" pa \"/\" public) token) (transcript a1))\n            (is (= 1 (count (filter #(re-find token-line %) @(:lines a1))))))\n          (when token\n            ;; A publishes and stops, so no head is reachable until every\n            ;; reader has parked: the first contact cannot race the install\n            (doseq [line publisher-lines] (type! a1 line))\n            (is (await-head-written a1 (dirs 0) exchange-ms) (transcript a1))\n            (stop! a1)\n            (is (.exists (io/file node-script))\n                (str \"the Node reader is required: \" node-script\n                     \" is absent; build it with `bb build:yin-repl-node`\"))\n            (let\n              [join (fn [label command dir]\n                      (let [p (spawn-stateful! label command\n                                               [\"dht\" \"join\" token \"--dir\" dir\n                                                \"--peer\" (peer x)])]\n                        (swap! procs conj p)\n                        p))\n               b (join \"reader-b-jvm\" (jvm-command) (dirs 1))\n               e (when (.exists (io/file node-script))\n                   (join \"reader-b-node\" [\"node\" node-script] (dirs 2)))\n               readers (remove nil? [b e])\n               _ (doseq [p readers] (first-contact-leg p))\n               ;; A comes back on the same port: its recovered HEAD is its\n               ;; board's first trace (5.4)\n               a (spawn! \"publisher-a-again\" (into a-args [\"--dht-port\"\n                                                           (str pa)]))]\n              (swap! procs conj a)\n              (testing \"A restarted on its port prints the same token\"\n                (is (= token (some->> (await-line a token-line startup-ms)\n                                      (re-find token-line)\n                                      second))\n                    (transcript a)))\n              (doseq [p readers] (follower-leg p principal))\n              (testing \"join saved --dht-follow\"\n                (is (str/includes? (slurp (str (dirs 1) \"/state.edn\"))\n                                   (str \":dht-follow [\\\"\" public \"@127.0.0.1:\"\n                                        pa \"\\\"]\"))))\n              (type! a \"(def f (fn [x] (+ x 4300)))\")\n              (type! a \"(require (quote yin.link))\")\n              (type! a \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))\")\n              (doseq [p readers] (moved-leg p))\n              (testing \"a reader restarted with A stopped still requires it\"\n                (stop! a)\n                (doseq [p readers] (stop! p))\n                (doseq [[label command dir] [[\"reader-b-jvm-again\" (jvm-command)\n                                              (dirs 1)]\n                                             (when e\n                                               [\"reader-b-node-again\"\n                                                [\"node\" node-script] (dirs 2)])]\n                        :when label]\n                  (let [p (spawn-stateful! label command [\"--dir\" dir])]\n                    (swap! procs conj p)\n                    (is (await-line p #\"dht: following ed25519:\\S+ at .*; installed head\"\n                                    startup-ms)\n                        (transcript p))\n                    (is (await-next p \"(require (quote my.lib))\"\n                                    #\"^(yin> )*'my\\.lib$\")\n                        (transcript p))\n                    (is (await-next p \"(my.lib/f 1)\" #\"^(yin> )*4301$\")\n                        (transcript p))))))))\n        (finally\n          (doseq [p @procs] (stop! p))\n          ((:stop! anchor))\n          (io/delete-file key-file true)\n          (run! delete-dir! dirs))))))\nFor \"fails without the fix\", I used one of two methods. For #1 and #3 I wrote the test first and watched it fail. For #2, #4, #5, #8 and #9 I temporarily reverted the fix, ran the test, saw it fail, and restored the fix.\n\n## Per item\n\n1. **P1: a socket left open after a startup refusal.** Reproduced: a truncated `heads.edn` left the socket bound and never closed (counter showed `{:bound 1}` only).\n   - **Change:** `open` now reads and parses `heads.edn` before the node binds. The part after the join moved into a new private `compose` function, and any failure there closes the joined node (`dht/close!`) before rethrowing.\n   - **Test:** `heads-edn-cases-are-refusals-as-data`, which now uses a recording bind seam and asserts binds equal closes in every refusal case. It failed before the fix.\n\n2. **P1: an overflowing port throws out of `startup`.** Reproduced: `NumberFormatException` escaped `startup`.\n   - **Change:** `parse-int` accepts at most 15 digits, so every host parses exactly and nothing can overflow. `--port` now goes through it too and is refused outside 0–65535; it previously called `Long/parseLong` directly.\n   - **Coverage:** every numeric flag shares `parse-int`. The test covers `--dht-follow`, `--dht-peer`, `--dht-port`, `--dht-max-inbound-bytes`, `--port`, a `dht join` token port and `--listen`.\n   - **Test:** `an-oversized-number-is-a-refusal-on-every-numeric-flag`. With the old regex it errored with `NumberFormatException`.\n\n3. **P2: only the first EDN form was read.** Reproduced: a trailing form and a truncated second form both read as a valid empty record.\n   - **Change:** the text is read inside a vector closed by a random keyword, and must come back as exactly the record plus that keyword. This works on every host with no host-specific reader.\n   - **Test:** new cases in `heads-edn-cases-are-refusals-as-data`: a trailing form, a truncated suffix, and an empty file.\n\n4. **P2: no size bound, no strict UTF-8.** Reproduced as described: a `0xff` byte inside a comment parsed, because the old read decoded leniently.\n   - **Change:** a bounded read on each host (at most `heads-max-bytes` + 1 bytes, with 1 MiB as the bound) and strict decoding on each host:\n     - JVM: a `CharsetDecoder` set to REPORT.\n     - Node: `TextDecoder` with `fatal`.\n     - Dart: `Utf8Decoder` with `allowMalformed false`.\n   - **Named refusals:** \"holds more than … bytes\" and \"not valid UTF-8\".\n   - **Test:** `heads-edn-is-bounded-and-strict-utf-8`, which also checks that comments and whitespace around a record still read, and that the socket is closed on the refusal. It failed with a lenient JVM decode.\n\n5. **P2: an overflowing refusal ring silenced reports for good.** Reproduced: the note reader stopped at the gap and kept its old cursor.\n   - **Change:** on a gap it now adopts the recovery cursor, prints that the oldest refusals were not reported, and drains what the ring still holds.\n   - **Test:** `deposit-refusals-past-the-ring-are-reported-lost-then-stay-visible` (65 notes → the \"lost\" line plus 64 reported, then a 66th is still shown). It failed with the old loop.\n\n6. **P2: the kill cases are simulated.** Following the Architect's ruling, I built no kill harness.\n   - **Change:** the kill cases are split out into `a-simulated-crash-restarts-at-the-head-heads-edn-holds`, with a comment stating the simulation.\n   - **New case:** a real `atomic-replace!` interrupted before its rename. It leaves the old `heads.edn` bytes exactly as they were and a stale temp file beside it. Startup ignores the temp file, and the next write replaces `heads.edn`.\n   - `the-write-precedes-the-install` now covers only the failed write and the retry.\n\n7. **P2: the process test raced the first contact.** Reproduced by reading the test, not by an observed failure; the race could fail correct behaviour.\n   - **Change:** A publishes and then stops. Each reader joins, switches VM, types the require, and is asserted parked with no answer yet. Only then does A restart on its own port (same token; its recovered HEAD is the board's first trace). Each parked require then completes with no further input.\n   - **Test:** `require-on-each-vm` gained an offset so each wait is for its own answer. The test passed with 40 assertions.\n\n8. **The moved line repeated.**\n   - **Change:** the moved set is computed before and after this step's installs. Only new name-and-address pairs print, and nothing is stored.\n   - **Test:** `a-move-is-reported-once-and-each-name-its-own`. Without the fix, alib printed 2 and then 3 times.\n\n9. **A failed dial was silent.**\n   - **Change:** one line per change of failure reason, not one per attempt:\n     - refused connection;\n     - no board for this principal (not-found);\n     - no answer;\n     - no dialer.\n   - The remembered reason clears when a dial attaches.\n   - **Test:** `a-dial-failure-prints-once-per-change`, for both nothing listening and a board of another principal. It failed with 4 lines each without the fix.\n\n10. **Docs** (`yin.repl.md`):\n    - (a) A record that refuses startup now says \"remove that record\", and the doc states the cost: that principal's floor is dropped, so rollback protection for it ends until a head is installed.\n    - (b) Publishers should use a fixed `--listen` port, because a reader's saved `--dht-follow` names it.\n    - (c) `dht join` is loopback only, so cross-machine readers still use `--dht-manifest` with `--dht-principal`.\n    - The doc also gains the new \"cannot follow\" line.\n\n11. **Ticks.** The unpersisted line now says \"ticks\"; asserted in `the-write-precedes-the-install`.\n\n**Beyond the list:**\n- The record-refusal message now names the cost too (\"…dropping its rollback floor\").\n- The `--port` refusal is new behaviour: a non-numeric `--port` used to throw a raw exception.\n- I did not touch the other Architect notes.\n\n## Commands and outcomes\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint` on `dht.cljc`, `main.cljc`, `dht_head_test.cljc`, `main_test.cljc` and `dht_process_test.clj`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- The 13-namespace JVM run (the 10 `yin.repl.*` and 3 `yin.vm.linker.head*` namespaces): **265 tests, 2,807 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.**\n- `clj -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`: **3 tests, 131 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.**\n- Revert checks:\n  - `main-test` without fix #2: 1 error.\n  - `dht-head-test` without fixes #4, #5, #8 and #9: 11 failures.\n  - Both were restored and re-run green.\n\n## Unresolved\n- **Possible design amendment:** design 5.7 says `<node dir>/heads.edn`, but the file lives in the store directory, as reported last round. If that sentence should change, it needs an amendment I didn't make.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
