{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-06 08:35:28 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-06 15:35:28 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a1103a-2d0e-7f82-b9a3-8f50d00edd21\n\nAll seven original findings are resolved:\n\n1. **Socket leak:** malformed EDN now binds nothing; a post-bind record refusal produced one bind and one socket close.\n2. **Numeric overflow:** oversized ports refuse as data. Leading zeros, signs, whitespace, Unicode digits, empty strings, and numeric flags were probed without raw parser exceptions.\n3. **Trailing EDN:** original malformed suffixes refuse. Dispatch/eval forms and closing-vector escapes also refused; complete reader discards remain valid EDN.\n4. **Size and UTF-8:** exactly 1 MiB passes; 1 MiB + 1 refuses. Invalid bytes, overlong sequences, and surrogate encodings refuse on JVM. Node/Dart execution remains pending.\n5. **Refusal-ring overflow:** 65 notes produce one loss message and 64 retained diagnostics; the next refusal remains visible.\n6. **Crash tests:** resolved under the Architect’s accepted simulation ruling. The tests cover interrupted atomic rename, unchanged old bytes, stale-temp recovery, and persistence before installation.\n7. **First-contact race:** resolved. Readers demonstrably park while the publisher is stopped, then complete after restart without further input.\n\nRemaining findings:\n\n- **P2 | src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:174 | evidence:** A named pipe at `heads.edn` blocks in the bounded reader. A focused JVM child reached `ENTERING-READ` and remained blocked until killed after 15 seconds. During startup, the directory lock has already been acquired. **Concrete fix:** reject non-regular targets before a potentially blocking open, handle symlinks explicitly, and validate the opened resource where supported. Add a bounded subprocess test for FIFO refusal.\n\n- **P2 | src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:431 | evidence:** Cleanup can replace the original startup refusal with a raw exception. Injecting a local-store close failure during an unfollowed-record refusal yielded `IOException(\"close failed\")`, no `ex-data`, one socket close, and two local-close attempts. The principal/record diagnostic was lost. **Concrete fix:** preserve the original refusal through cleanup failures and close through the node once ownership transfers; avoid closing `base` again. Test throwing socket/store close seams.\n\nNo repository files edited; verified suites were not repeated.\n\nBlocked on the two remaining P2 findings and the Node and Dart lanes passing."}}
